"H6828","lemma":"צָפוֹן","tr":"tsa·phon","gloss":"north","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":153},{"base":"H7097","lemma":"קָצֶה","tr":"qa·tseh","gloss":"end","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":97},{"base":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","tr":"a·lah","gloss":"to ascend: rise","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":889},{"base":"H2022","lemma":"הַר","tr":"har","gloss":"mountain: mount","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":546},{"base":"H1173","lemma":"בַּעֲלָה","tr":"ba·a·lah","gloss":"(Mount) Baalah","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":6},{"base":"H8388","lemma":"תָּאַר","tr":"ta·ar","gloss":"to border","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":8}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then it went down to the foot of the hill that faces the Valley of Hinnom at the northern end of the Valley of Rephaim and ran down the Valley of Hinnom toward the southern slope of the Jebusites and downward to En-rogel.","from":8},{"book":"NUM","chapter":34,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"cross south of the Ascent of Akrabbim, continue to Zin, and go south of Kadesh-barnea. Then it will go on to Hazar-addar and proceed to Azmon,","from":3},{"book":"NUM","chapter":34,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"where it will turn from Azmon, join the Brook of Egypt, and end at the Sea.","from":4},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":63,"verseEnd":63,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But the descendants of Judah could not drive out the Jebusites living in Jerusalem. So to this day the Jebusites live there among the descendants of Judah.","from":8},{"book":"JDG","chapter":14,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"One day Samson went down to Timnah, where he saw a young Philistine woman.","from":10},{"book":"1CH","chapter":13,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"David and all Israel went up to Baalah of Judah (that is, Kiriath-jearim) to bring up from there the ark of God the LORD, who is enthroned between the cherubim—the ark that is called by the Name.","from":9},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The latter five came as allies to the Valley of Siddim (that is, the Salt Sea).","from":2},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then they turned back to invade En-mishpat (that is, Kadesh), and they conquered the whole territory of the Amalekites, as well as the Amorites who lived in Hazazon-tamar.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"13-19":{"people":[{"id":"caleb-h3612g","name":"Caleb","kind":"person","brief":"Joshua's compatriot","count":5,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"anak-h6061","name":"Anak","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Arba","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"arba-h0704","name":"Arba","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"jephunneh-h3312g","name":"Jephunneh","kind":"person","brief":"Caleb's father","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"ahiman-h0289g","name":"Ahiman","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"sheshai-h8344","name":"Sheshai","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"talmai-h8526g","name":"Talmai","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Anak","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"achsah-h5915g","name":"Achsah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Iru","count":2,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"kenaz-h7073i","name":"Kenaz","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Othniel","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"othniel-h6274","name":"Othniel","kind":"person","brief":"A Judge","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"places":[{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"debir-h1688a","name":"Debir","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"negeb-h5045g","name":"Negeb","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":19}],"words":[{"base":"H3612","lemma":"כָּלֵב","tr":"ka·lev","gloss":"Caleb","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":35},{"base":"H7158","lemma":"קִרְיַת־סֵ֫פֶר","tr":"qir·yat san·nah","gloss":"Kiriath-sannah","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":10},{"base":"H6061","lemma":"עֲנָק","tr":"a·naq","gloss":"Anak","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":9},{"base":"H1543","lemma":"גֻּלָּה","tr":"gul·lah","gloss":"bowl","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":15},{"base":"H5915","lemma":"עַכְסָה","tr":"akh·sah","gloss":"Achsah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H1688","lemma":"דְּבִיר","tr":"de·vir","gloss":"Debir","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"H7153","lemma":"קִרְיַת אַרְבַּע","tr":"qir·yat ar·ba","gloss":"Kiriath-arba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":121},{"base":"H5942","lemma":"עִלִּי","tr":"il·li","gloss":"upper","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6795","lemma":"צָנַח","tr":"tsa·nach","gloss":"to descend","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":24,"verse":64,"verseEnd":64,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And when Rebekah looked up and saw Isaac, she got down from her camel","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":33,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Please accept my gift that was brought to you, because God has been gracious to me and I have all I need.” So Jacob pressed him until he accepted.","from":19},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":22,"verseEnd":23,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They went up through the Negev and came to Hebron, where Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai, the descendants of Anak, dwelled. It had been built seven years before Zoan in Egypt. When they came to the Valley of Eshcol, they cut down a branch with a single cluster of grapes, which they carried on a pole between two men. They also took some pomegranates and figs.","from":14},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Caleb quieted the people before Moses and said, “We must go up and take possession of the land, for we can certainly conquer it!”","from":13},{"book":"NUM","chapter":14,"verse":23,"verseEnd":24,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"not one will ever see the land that I swore to give their fathers. None of those who have treated Me with contempt will see it. But because My servant Caleb has a different spirit and has followed Me wholeheartedly, I will bring him into the land he has entered, and his descendants will inherit it.","from":13},{"book":"NUM","chapter":32,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"not one except Caleb son of Jephunneh the Kenizzite and Joshua son of Nun—because they did follow the LORD wholeheartedly.’","from":17},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":34,"verseEnd":36,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When the LORD heard your words, He grew angry and swore an oath, saying, “Not one of the men of this evil generation shall see the good land I swore to give your fathers, except Caleb son of Jephunneh. He will see it, and I will give him and his descendants the land on which he has set foot, because he followed the LORD wholeheartedly.”","from":13},{"book":"DEU","chapter":33,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And concerning Judah he said: “O LORD, hear the cry of Judah and bring him to his people. With his own hands he defends his cause, but may You be a help against his foes.”","from":19}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2},{"id":"judges-era","title":"Judges era and the road to David","people":2}]},"20-63":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":3,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"jebusites-h2983g","name":"Jebusites","kind"